OAI ZMQ radio (pin 2b69bde6): an RX digital gain, zmq.[n].rx_gain_db.
The ZMQ path has no AGC: received samples reach the UE PHY at the level the
far end transmits. The UE fixed-point receive chain is sized for about
TARGET_RX_POWER (50 dB digital power); an OCUDU gNB at its default 12 dB
back-off arrives near 55 dB, and 64QAM PDSCH NACKs 69-89% (rank 1 and
rank 2) although the channel estimate and FFT are clean (SPARK_MILESTONES.md
S12). rx_gain_db scales the float->int16 conversion like the RF receive gain
of a radio; 0 (default) leaves it unchanged.
Apply in the OAI source root: patch -p1 < oai-zmq-rx-gain.patch

--- a/radio/zmq/zmq_radio.cpp
+++ b/radio/zmq/zmq_radio.cpp
@@ -41,17 +41,28 @@
